    "created_at": "2017-05-01T20:36:53Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-05-01T20:36:53Z",
    "body": "In this particular case I would advocate for a static method like either ImageBitmap.getSupportedOptions() or ImageBitmap.isOptionSupported(). The reason is that developers need to know before deciding to use ImageBitmap at all whether it's going to work as they expect. For WebGL developers, if the imageOrientation attribute is unsupported, they need to fall back to using HTMLImageElement to load their texture resources. Creating a dummy ImageBitmap is for this purpose will make web applications' startup sequence more complex.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
