    "updated_at": "2017-05-25T01:25:08Z",
    "body": "We keep bumping up against this problem in various APIs.  Is it really that much harder to agree on some [general-purpose compiler-automated pattern in WebIDL](https://github.com/heycam/webidl/issues/107) that we can start opting new dictionary types into, instead of [continuing](http://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-main/getusermedia.html#widl-MediaDevices-getSupportedConstraints-MediaTrackSupportedConstraints) to add one-off APIs to the web for this?\r\n\r\nI still really want to go back and add feature detection to `EventListenerOptions` but there's really nowhere good to hang a 'getSupportedOptions` method in that case.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
